# Roles and responsibilities: {{ engagement.name }}

The platform asks for a small number of named people at {{ client.name }}. Please confirm or nominate each role in the platform. One person can hold more than one role, but nobody can approve an item they prepared.

| Role | Required | What they do |
|---|---|---|
| Chief AI Compliance Officer | Yes | Leads the engagement for {{ client.name }}. Approves the inventory, responses to findings and any public summary. {% if contacts.caico.name %}Currently: {{ contacts.caico.name }}.{% endif %} |
| Client Admin | Yes | Adds departments and users and assigns roles. Has no access to audit content. {% if contacts.client_admin.name %}Currently: {{ contacts.client_admin.name }}.{% endif %} |
| Executive Sponsor | Optional | Signs the management representation and accepts the remediation plan. If not appointed, the Chief AI Compliance Officer signs. |
| Data Protection Officer | Optional | Reviews data categories for higher-risk uses of AI and the privacy of the employee attestation. If not appointed, the Chief AI Compliance Officer covers this. |
| Department Compliance Lead | Yes, one per department | Reviews and approves the AI tools and uses of AI in their department and responds to findings for it. |
| Contributor | Optional | Prepares AI tool and use-case entries and uploads evidence for their department, or for one AI system. |

Employees do not need an account. They answer a short attestation through a link. People named as users of higher-risk AI receive a separate link to confirm their training and oversight responsibilities.

